{#- ============================================================
    THE master template. One template every page uses.
    A page supplies front-matter (hero + an ordered list of
    `blocks`), and this renders them all in the unified .story
    frame. Change this file -> every page using it changes.

    DESIGN RULE: max ~100 words per panel. Each screen is ONE composed
    idea you could screenshot in isolation. If a section runs long, split
    it into two panels rather than cramming -- there is no scroll within a
    panel by design. Every screen (hero, blocks, footer) is a uniform
    .story panel so behaviour is identical on every device.

    ARCHITECTURE -- proper full-page scroller:
      <nav>            position:fixed, floats OVER everything.
      <div .story-scroll>   the ONE scroll container. It owns the
                       scrollbar and the snap (height:100svh,
                       overflow-y:scroll, scroll-snap-type). Because
                       snap lives here -- not on <html> -- the fixed
                       nav can never be captured by it (the Firefox
                       sticky-in-snap bug is structurally impossible).
        <section .story>    each panel is exactly 100svh, snap-align
                       start, content flex-centred. No nav-offset
                       maths: the nav floats, panels are full-height.
        <div .story-tail>   trailing non-snap region (SEO prose +
                       footer). Scrolls normally after the panels.

    Front-matter contract:
      hero: { eyebrow, heading, lede?, actions?[{label,href,style}], video? }
        EYEBROW IS THE HOUSE STYLE: every hero opens with a short eyebrow
        (small uppercase blue label) above the heading, then heading, then
        lede, then actions. The homepage is the reference. Always set an
        eyebrow so heros stay consistent across the site -- a section tag
        ("Pricing", "Support"), a category ("Guide . Electrical"), a market
        ("France"), or a punchy line ("No app. No paperwork.").
      blocks: [ ordered list, each { type: ..., feature?, ...fields } ]
        feature: true -> paint this ONE block as the gradient brand band
                         (white text). Use at most once per page.
        types:
          - prose:   { eyebrow?, heading?, text|html, alt? }
          - split:   { eyebrow?, heading, text, reverse?, alt? }
          - steps:   { eyebrow?, heading, items:[{title,text}], video?, alt? }
          - cards:   { eyebrow?, heading, items:[{kicker,title,text,href}], alt? }
          - tags:    { eyebrow?, heading, text?, items:[{label,href,strong?}], alt? }
          - cta:     { eyebrow?, heading, text?, actions:[{label,href,style?}], alt? }
          - raw:     { html, alt? }   (escape hatch for bespoke content)
      (footerCta in front-matter renders the closing CTA as today.)
      Free-form page body (the {{ content }}) renders inside .story-tail.
   ============================================================ -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ seo.lang or 'en' }}">
{% include "partials/head.njk" %}
<body class="{{ bodyClass or 'page-story' }}">
{% include "partials/nav.njk" %}
<main class="story-scroll">

{%- if hero %}
<section id="top" class="story story-hero">
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if hero.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ hero.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h1 class="story-h1">{{ hero.heading | safe }}</h1>
        {%- if hero.lede %}<p class="story-lede">{{ hero.lede | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- if hero.actions %}
        <div class="story-actions">
            {%- for a in hero.actions %}
            <a href="{{ a.href }}" class="btn {{ a.style or 'btn-primary' }}">{{ a.label }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if hero.actionNote %}<p class="story-action-note">{{ hero.actionNote }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- if hero.video %}
    <div class="story-media-hero story-video-embed">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ hero.video }}?rel=0" title="Quickler walkthrough" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#- Alternating colour rhythm so each reel panel is visually distinct and
    "instagrammable" on its own: hero is white (index 0), then panels
    alternate gradient / white / gradient / white down the page. A block can
    still force its look with feature:true (gradient), alt:true (tinted) or
    plain:true (white). The auto-rhythm uses loop.index (1-based): odd ->
    gradient band, even -> white. -#}
{%- for b in blocks %}
{%- if b.feature %}{% set altcls = "story-feature" %}
{%- elif b.plain %}{% set altcls = "" %}
{%- elif b.alt %}{% set altcls = "story-alt" %}
{%- elif loop.index is odd %}{% set altcls = "story-feature" %}
{%- else %}{% set altcls = "" %}{% endif %}
{%- if b.type == "prose" %}
{#- bgImage: a full-bleed photo behind this panel with a dark scrim over it so
    the text stays legible. The panel forces the white-on-dark text styling
    (story-photo reuses .story-feature's white text rules) regardless of the
    alternating colour rhythm. -#}
<section class="story {{ 'story-photo' if b.bgImage else altcls }}"{% if b.bgImage %} style="--bg-photo: url('{{ b.bgImage }}'){% if b.bgDim %}; --scrim-edge: {{ b.bgDim }}; --scrim-mid: {{ b.bgDim - 0.08 }}{% endif %}"{% endif %}>
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- if b.heading %}<h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>{% endif %}
        {%- if b.html %}{{ b.html | safe }}{% else %}<p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ b.text | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "split" %}
<section class="story {{ 'story-photo' if b.bgImage else altcls }}"{% if b.bgImage %} style="--bg-photo: url('{{ b.bgImage }}'){% if b.bgDim %}; --scrim-edge: {{ b.bgDim }}; --scrim-mid: {{ b.bgDim - 0.08 }}{% endif %}"{% endif %}>
    {%- if b.bgImage %}
    {#- Photo-backed split: full-panel photo + scrim (like prose). The media
        column is dropped; copy centres so the text reads over the photo. -#}
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
        <p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ b.text | safe }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="story-split {{ 'story-split-reverse' if b.reverse }}">
        <div class="story-copy">
            {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
            <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
            <p class="story-text">{{ b.text | safe }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="story-media" role="img" aria-label="{{ b.mediaAlt or '' }}"></div>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "steps" %}
<section class="story {{ altcls }}">
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
        <ol class="story-steps">
            {%- for it in b.items %}
            <li class="story-step"><span class="story-step-n">{{ loop.index }}</span><h3>{{ it.title }}</h3><p>{{ it.text }}</p></li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
        {%- if b.video %}
        <div class="story-video-embed">
            <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ b.video }}?rel=0" title="Quickler walkthrough" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "cards" %}
<section class="story {{ altcls }}">
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
        <div class="story-cards" style="--n: {{ b.items | length }}">
            {%- for it in b.items %}
            <a class="story-card" href="{{ it.href }}">{%- if it.kicker %}<span class="story-card-kicker">{{ it.kicker }}</span>{% endif %}<h3>{{ it.title }}</h3><p>{{ it.text }}</p></a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "tags" %}
<section class="story {{ altcls }}">
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
        {%- if b.text %}<p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ b.text | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
        <div class="story-tags">
            {%- for it in b.items %}
            <a href="{{ it.href }}" class="story-tag {{ 'story-tag-strong' if it.strong }}">{{ it.label }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "cta" %}
<section class="story story-cta {{ 'story-photo' if b.bgImage else altcls }}"{% if b.bgImage %} style="--bg-photo: url('{{ b.bgImage }}'){% if b.bgDim %}; --scrim-edge: {{ b.bgDim }}; --scrim-mid: {{ b.bgDim - 0.08 }}{% endif %}"{% endif %}>
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>
        {%- if b.text %}<p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ b.text | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- if b.actions %}
        <div class="story-actions">
            {%- for a in b.actions %}
            <a href="{{ a.href }}" class="btn {{ a.style or 'btn-primary' }}">{{ a.label }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "video" %}
<section class="story story-video-panel {{ altcls }}">
    <div class="story-inner">
        {%- if b.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- if b.heading %}<h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading | safe }}</h2>{% endif %}
        {#- Lite facade: NO YouTube iframe loads on page load (the player is
            ~1.5MB+ of JS over a dozen requests -- the slow-load cause). Show
            just the thumbnail + play button; js/persist-video.js swaps in the
            real autoplaying iframe on click, then keeps it playing as you
            scroll past. -#}
        <div class="story-video-embed yt-lite" data-yt="{{ b.video }}" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play the Quickler walkthrough video">
            <img class="yt-lite-thumb" src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/{{ b.video }}/hqdefault.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="480" height="360">
            <button type="button" class="yt-lite-play" aria-label="Play video"><svg viewBox="0 0 68 48" width="68" height="48" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#f00" d="M66.5 7.7a8 8 0 0 0-5.6-5.7C56 .6 34 .6 34 .6S12 .6 7.1 2a8 8 0 0 0-5.6 5.7A83 83 0 0 0 0 24a83 83 0 0 0 1.5 16.3 8 8 0 0 0 5.6 5.7C12 47.4 34 47.4 34 47.4s22 0 26.9-1.4a8 8 0 0 0 5.6-5.7A83 83 0 0 0 68 24a83 83 0 0 0-1.5-16.3z"/><path fill="#fff" d="M27 34l18-10-18-10z"/></svg></button>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{%- elif b.type == "raw" %}
<section class="story {{ altcls }}"><div class="story-inner">{{ b.html | safe }}</div></section>
{%- elif b.type == "pricing" %}
{#- Pricing block: renders the bundle/plan grid from the single source of truth
    (src/_data/pricing.js) via the {% pricingCards %} shortcode. A pricing change
    in that data file updates every page using this block. eyebrow/heading/intro
    are optional overrides. -#}
<section class="story {{ altcls }}"><div class="story-inner">
    <p class="story-eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow or "Monthly bundles" }}</p>
    <h2 class="story-h2">{{ b.heading or "Pick the bundle that fits." }}</h2>
    {%- if b.intro %}<p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ b.intro }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% pricingCards %}
    <p class="story-text story-text-centre">{{ pricing.overflowLine }} <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Talk to us</a>. {{ pricing.billing }}</p>
</div></section>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{#- Article as REEL PANELS, in the SAME look + rhythm as the home page:
    pink (gradient) / white / photo, alternating, centred cards. The article's
    sections become full-screen snap panels that continue the reel. Each panel
    still holds full crawlable text (SEO preserved). The colour rhythm continues
    from the page's blocks (offset by `blocks | length`) so the alternation does
    not reset. Every Nth panel gets the page's photo (articlePhoto) so the
    pink/white/photo pattern matches home. `articlePanels`: list of
    { eyebrow?, heading?, html, kind? }. -#}
{%- if articlePanels %}
{%- set base = (blocks | length) or 0 %}
{%- for ap in articlePanels %}
{%- set n = base + loop.index %}
{#- photo every 3rd panel (if the page has an articlePhoto); else alternate
    gradient (odd) / white (even), exactly like the blocks loop. -#}
{%- set usePhoto = articlePhoto and (loop.index0 % 3 == 2) and ap.kind != 'lede' and ap.kind != 'takeaways' %}
{%- if usePhoto %}{% set acls = "story-photo" %}
{%- elif ap.kind == 'lede' %}{% set acls = "" %}
{%- elif n is odd %}{% set acls = "story-feature" %}
{%- else %}{% set acls = "" %}{% endif %}
<section class="story story-article story-article-{{ ap.kind or 'default' }} {{ acls }}"{% if usePhoto %} style="--bg-photo: url('{{ articlePhoto }}'); --scrim-edge: 0.92; --scrim-mid: 0.84"{% endif %}>
    <div class="story-inner story-article-inner">
        {%- if ap.eyebrow %}<p class="story-eyebrow">{{ ap.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        {%- if ap.heading %}<h2 class="story-h2">{{ ap.heading | safe }}</h2>{% endif %}
        <div class="story-article-body">{{ ap.html | safe }}</div>
    </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{#- Related guides -- internal-linking cluster. A final reel panel that links to
    the 3-4 topically-closest guides. Spreads link equity (Google reads tight
    topical clusters as authority) and keeps readers on-site. Rendered in the
    reel rhythm: it continues the alternation so it never clashes with the panel
    before it. `relatedLinks`: [{ label, href, blurb? }] in front-matter. -#}
{%- if relatedLinks and relatedLinks | length %}
{%- set rn = ((blocks | length) or 0) + ((articlePanels | length) or 0) + 1 %}
<section class="story story-article story-related {{ 'story-feature' if rn is odd }}">
    <div class="story-inner story-article-inner">
        <p class="story-eyebrow">Keep reading</p>
        <h2 class="story-h2">Related guides</h2>
        <ul class="story-related-list">
            {%- for r in relatedLinks %}
            <li><a href="{{ r.href }}">{{ r.label }}</a>{% if r.blurb %} <span class="story-related-blurb">{{ r.blurb }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#- Optional long-form SEO region (LEGACY fallback for pages not yet converted
    to articlePanels). Raw HTML article rendered as a styled scroll region after
    the reel panels, before the footer. Crawlable, visible, indexable. -#}
{%- if seoBody and not articlePanels %}
<section class="story-seo" aria-label="More detail">
    <div class="story-seo-inner">
        {{ seoBody | safe }}
    </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#- Free-form page body (the {{ content }}) renders as its own non-snap region
    BEFORE the footer, like seoBody -- so a page can supply a long list/article
    in its body and it scrolls normally instead of being crammed in the footer. -#}
{%- if content %}
{{ content | safe }}
{%- endif %}

{#- Footer is its OWN reel panel -- a uniform full-screen .story like every
    other section, so it behaves identically on every device (no special
    'tail' region that broke on mobile). -#}
<section class="story story-footer">
{% include "partials/footer.njk" %}
</section>

</main>

{#- Structured data (JSON-LD), generated from content already on the page so it
    can never drift from what the reader sees. Organization + WebSite are emitted
    on every story page (site identity for Google's knowledge panel and AI
    crawlers). FAQPage is emitted only when an articlePanels FAQ block exists
    (parsed from its <h3>/<p> pairs) -> FAQ rich results. Article is emitted for
    guide pages (those with articlePanels) -> Article rich results. A page can
    still override with its own seo.jsonld in the head. -#}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "Quickler",
  "legalName": "{{ site.company }}",
  "url": "{{ site.domain }}",
  "logo": "{{ site.domain }}/assets/icons/apple-touch-icon.png",
  "email": "{{ site.email }}",
  "sameAs": ["{{ site.linkedin }}"]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "name": "Quickler",
  "url": "{{ site.domain }}"
}
</script>
{%- if articlePanels %}
{%- set faqLd = articlePanels | faqSchema %}
{%- if faqLd %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{{ faqLd | safe }}
</script>
{%- endif %}
{%- set articleLd = seo | articleSchema %}
{%- if articleLd %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{{ articleLd | safe }}
</script>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

{%- for s in scripts %}
<script src="{{ s }}"></script>
{%- endfor %}
</body>
</html>
